{
  "about": "Email services recognisable from a domain's own DNS. One block per vendor; imported from dns-audit (MIT) at fac9e2e. Hostname patterns match the host itself or any name under it, and the longest match wins. Every pattern is an entry with its value and a proof: a live domain that publishes it, the record name (or, for a website host, the page) as found, and the date it was checked. Networks are autonomous system numbers a service owns outright; shared clouds are listed under rules.cloud_networks and never credited to a service. Each selectors entry names a vendor's DKIM selectors with their source and a proof; a fixed shape with several names takes a list of proofs, one per name in order. Hints are MX and SPF values the vendor's customers publish, with the pages that list them. Patterns not yet proven wait in vendors_pending.json, which Sendermap never reads.",
  "categories": [
    "Mailbox",
    "Security gateway",
    "Marketing",
    "Transactional",
    "Support and CRM",
    "Commerce and apps",
    "DMARC reporting"
  ],
